View-aware glass: a pane drawn somewhere else is damaged, watched and culled there.

A view that draws the windows of several workspaces somewhere else and smaller
(stackzoom, through the renderer's modifier, patch 0007) had the glass still
judge everything by where the windows really are:

- A pane's damage (a fresh sample wanted, the focus light, frost) went to the
  window's own box: at full size, in a part of the monitor the pane is not in,
  and not where it is. With the view redrawing the whole monitor on every
  frame nobody saw that; with the view damaging only what changed, it is the
  difference between one pane and half the screen. The monitor is now damaged
  where the pane was last drawn.
- A window on a workspace that is not shown was marked for a fresh sample by
  commits at its place on the shown one (every workspace of a monitor has its
  windows at the same places). It is not behind any of them: skipped.
- A pane drawn wholly off the frame (a column of a row running past the
  screen) was still sampled, blurred and drawn: skipped.
- The pass was told the window's own box for a pane that needs a fresh
  sample, and asked with that box every pane claimed one on every frame (the
  sample is sized by the drawn box): told and asked with the drawn box.
- A layer's sample region, already cut to its own monitor, is damaged on that
  monitor directly instead of through the renderer's damageBox(): the same
  damage, but a box handed to the renderer says nothing of what it belongs to,
  and such a view has to take it for a window's and damage it in every row.

Outside such a view nothing changes but the second point.

